      "notes": "Purpose: Use structured breathing for autonomic regulation, breath control, and recovery support without mixing it analytically with meditation skill training.\n\nGoals: physiological_downshift: Practice breathing patterns that reliably reduce perceived activation and support calm recovery. recovery_support: Use low-strain breathwork after hard training or stressful days to support readiness for subsequent training. breath_control: Progress breath control without turning breathwork into max-effort breath-hold training. pattern_comparison: Keep practice types distinct enough that later experiments can compare resonance, extended exhale, box breathing, and CO2 tolerance.\n\nMeasurement hooks: pre_session_window: Optional quiet baseline before the session. post_session_window: Optional quiet window after the session to measure acute change. next_morning_window: Optional next-morning recovery/readiness comparison. training_context: Log whether the day included hard training, long run, easy run, rest, poor sleep, high stress, caffeine, or alcohol.\n\nProgression: breathing_is_not_the_bottleneck: Do not progress breathwork merely because the current pattern is easy. calm_before_intensity: Only progress a pattern if it remains smooth, calm, and non-strained. harder_patterns_are_sparse: Use 5/5/5/5 box breathing and progressed CO2 work sparingly, not daily. recovery_days_are_not_tests: After hard training, prioritize extended exhale or resonance breathing over challenging CO2 work. separate_from_meditation: Do not combine breathwork ratings with meditation-skill ratings when analyzing effects.\n\nCompletion criteria: minimum_adherence: Complete at least 20 of 28 assigned days. resonance_exposure: Complete at least 6 resonance breathing sessions. extended_exhale_exposure: Complete at least 6 extended-exhale sessions. harder_breathwork_exposure: Complete at least 2 box progression or CO2 progression sessions, but do not force completion if strain is high. review_completion: Complete at least 3 of 4 weekly reviews.\n\nAfter four weeks: resonance_breathing_produces_reliable_downshift: Keep resonance breathing as the standard comparison and recovery-priming pattern. extended_exhale_improves_evening_recovery: Keep extended exhale as the default evening or post-hard-training breathwork. box_5_5_5_5_adds_no_value_over_4_4_4_4: Stop progressing box breathing and keep the simpler version only as a short composure tool. co2_progressions_create_strain_or_activation: Drop CO2 progression and keep only the easy 4/6/4 pattern occasionally. harder_breathwork_feels_satisfying_but_does_not_help_recovery: Treat harder breathwork as optional skill work, not a recovery intervention.",
